This repository is licensed in two parts.

The book
--------
The prose - everything under `_chapters/`, plus `index.md` and the rendered
site and PDF built from them - is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. See `LICENSE-BOOK`.

In short: share it and adapt it, including commercially, as long as you give
credit and license what you build on it the same way.

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The code
--------
Everything under `examples/` and `tools/`, and the code samples printed inside
the chapters, are licensed under the MIT License. See `LICENSE-CODE`.

In short: use them in your own projects, under any license, with no obligation
beyond keeping the copyright notice.

The split is deliberate. ShareAlike on a code sample would be a trap: nobody
should have to relicense their application because they copied ten lines out of
a book that exists to be copied from.

Site furniture - `_layouts/`, `assets/` - is MIT, as code.

